+#: The one endpoint whose ceiling is not its platform's number.
+#:
+#: Measured 2026-10-15 against the live endpoint with an imported identity:
+#:
+#:     count=30  ->  a full page, ``has_more`` true
+#:     count=31  ->  an empty ``data``, ``has_more`` false
+#:
+#: Same failure shape as TikTok's 35 above, and the more dangerous half of it:
+#: a search that is refused reads as "your keyword matched nothing", so a caller
+#: asking for 31 is told the keyword has no results at all. Douyin's ceiling for
+#: its paged lists is 50, which is why this cannot live in the platform table -
+#: the number belongs to the endpoint.
+#:
+#: A platform without an entry falls back to its platform ceiling; only Douyin
+#: serves this operation (TikTok's adapter raises ``UnsupportedContent``), so
+#: the fallback is what a future platform would want until it is measured.
+MAX_SEARCH_PAGE_SIZE: Final[Mapping[Platform, int]] = MappingProxyType(
+    {
+        Platform.DOUYIN: 30,
+    }
+)
+
+
+def max_search_page_size(platform: Platform) -> int:
+    """The page-size ceiling for keyword search on ``platform``."""
+    return MAX_SEARCH_PAGE_SIZE.get(platform, max_page_size(platform))
+
+
+__all__ = ["MAX_PAGE_SIZE", "MAX_SEARCH_PAGE_SIZE", "max_page_size", "max_search_page_size"]
